      "writtenOn": "2024-09-25T02:58:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Traversing the proc-\u003enodes is very complicated because of the lock ordering. I believe we _could_ invert the order which would simplify this loop but it would also complicate other cases.\n\nAs it stands, I believe we could miss newly added nodes but the same applies if we were able to hold the inner_lock throughout. What I mean is new nodes could be added _after_ we exit the loop too and we\u0027d miss those.\n\nHowever, this wouldn\u0027t be a problem. When the reference adds a frozen notification for this new node (which we missed here), it will still get the current frozen status per the logic in `binder_request_freeze_notification()`.",
      "parentUuid": "ad5bc544_64089f21",
      "revId": "7eda12555b81c97036d3a8bd600ad2252e4fa6f4",
